cuments faster in daily operations</h1> <p>A digital agricultural office does not start with as much software as possible. It starts by connecting recurring documents, tasks and responsibilities in a traceable workflow.</p> <a class="button button-gold" href="/en/contact">Free initial call</a> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Starting point</span> <h2>Where friction develops</h2> <p>When email, local folders, specialist software, spreadsheets and paper run in parallel, search time and duplicate work grow. The first step is therefore a factual review of one real workflow.</p> </div> <div class="card-grid three"> <article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">01</span><h3>Document search</h3><p>Records, invoices, orders or field documents are stored in several places and cannot be found reliably.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">02</span><h3>Duplicate entry</h3><p>Information is transferred again from paper, email or specialist software into spreadsheets and other systems.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="card-index">03</span><h3>Unclear handovers</h3><p>It is not clear who checks, completes, approves or provides a document for the next step.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="container"> <div class="section-heading"> <span class="section-kicker">Approach</span> <h2>A small, operational starting point</h2> <p>IBS-Saxony reviews one specific document workflow and organizes it so that the next actionable step becomes visible.</p> </div> <div class="step-grid"> <article class="step-card"><span>01</span><h3>Select a workflow</h3><p>We choose one recurring process that currently creates search time, questions or duplicate entry.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>02</span><h3>Organize sources and roles</h3><p>Document locations, people, systems and necessary handovers are mapped in a clear way.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span>03</span><h3>Define a starting measure</h3><p>You receive a limited next work block. Paid work only starts after scope and price range have been confirmed.</p></article> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section section-soft"> <div class="container narrow service-card related-card"> <span class="section-kicker">Subject context</span> <h2>Public subject context</h2> <p>Saxony&#39;s State Office for Environment, Agriculture and Geology describes document management as part of the digital agricultural office. IBS-Saxony adds practical process and implementation work for the individual business.</p> <a class="text-link" href="https://www.landwirtschaft.sachsen.de/digitales-agrarbuero-dokumentenmanagement-69902.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LfULG: digital agricultural office and document management (German)</a> </div> </section> <section class="section section-dark"> <div class="container narrow"> <span class="section-kicker">Boundaries</span> <p>IBS-Saxony does not provide legal, tax, funding or other binding professional advice. Retention, evidence and funding questions remain with the respective qualified specialists.</p> <a class="text-link" href="/en/process-documentation-regional-businesses">Process documentation for regional businesses</a> </div> </section> <section class="section final-cta"> <div class="container"> <span class="section-kicker">Next step</span> <h2>Review one document workflow together</h2> <p>In the free process call, we select one real workflow and clarify whether a small operational start makes sense.</p> <a class="button button-gold" href="/en/contact">Free initial call</a> </div> </section>  </main> <footer class="site-footer"> <div class="footer-grid"> <div> <img class="footer-logo" src="/assets/logo-ibs-saxony-white.png" alt="IBS-Saxony"> <p>Process optimization, systems integration and digital tools for companies in Saxony.</p> <detai